nodecode-channel-onebot is a rewrite of mario841859784's mario841859784/hermes-plugin-onebot:

  https://github.com/mario841859784/hermes-plugin-onebot
  commit 086dd7e5c13004e41301f5cea1f352c46b0f3c50
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 mario841859784 (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the lane as a whole -- talking to a OneBot 11 bridge's
HTTP API for the groups an account is in and the newest messages of each,
deciding which of them were addressed to the bot (an at of its own QQ
number, or a reply to one of its own messages, in a group; anything in a
private chat; free-response groups and a mention switch for the rest),
answering through (send_group_msg) and (send_private_msg), reading both
shapes a OneBot message comes in (the segment array and the CQ code string,
with its &amp; &#91; &#93; escapes), defusing a CQ code the model wrote so an
answer cannot ping a group, and keeping a read position per chat so a
restart does not answer the same message twice. All of it was reimplemented
in Common Lisp against Nodecode's channel cell contract, so the chats,
lanes, gate, cards and delivery are the channel kit's rather than the
plugin's own gateway plumbing.

What was left out and why: the Hermes gateway adapter class and its config
plumbing are the harness's own and became a channels.onebot section. The
plugin's WebSocket transport -- the reverse-WS server it hosts inside the
gateway, and the forward-WS client -- is replaced by the bridge's HTTP API,
which every bridge above serves on the same port as its WebSocket and which
needs no long-lived socket of ours; the read position therefore lives in
the running process rather than in a data file, and a restart answers
nothing that was said while it was down instead of catching it up. The qq_*
tools (send image, voice, video, file, forward; the raw NapCat API call;
group history) are not carried as tools: the lane answers what the host
hands it, and a model reaches the bridge directly for anything else. Inbound
pictures are not downloaded or downscaled for a vision tool, the text-to-image
renderer (fonttools and CJK fonts) is not carried, and the cron home channel
is the host cell's delivery, not this folder's.
